Addresses the "- [ ] Spawn new threads when executing a GDSAlgorithm in task scheduler." item of: https://github.com/kuzudb/kuzu/issues/3717. This is a simple change that adds a new boolean `launchNewWorkerThread` argument to TaskScheduler::scheduleTaskAndWaitOrError function to spawn a new thread or not. By default this argument is false. GDSUtils sets it to true when launching GDSTasks.

I can't think of tests for this but wrote the following program to test that the change behaves as expected in several ways. 
```
int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
